==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*süü}}, from {{inh|fi|urj-pro|*süxe}} or {{m|urj-pro|*süje}}. Cognates include {{cog|et|süü}}, {{cog|kpv|сі}}. The sense "reason, cause" (and those akin to it) was originally figurative.

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[fibre]], [[filament]]
#: {{syn|fi|kuitu|säie}}
# {{lb|fi|usually|in plural}} [[grain]] {{gloss|linear texture of a material or surface}}
#: {{ux|fi|Koivun '''syyt''' ovat yleensä suorat.|The '''grain''' of birch is usually straight.}}
# {{lb|fi|cytology}} [[fibre]] {{gloss|long tubular cell found in bodily tissue}}
# [[cause]], [[reason]] {{gloss|source or reason of an event or action; goal, aim, principle}} {{+obj|fi|ill<for>|inf3 ill<to do>}}
#: {{coi|fi|turman '''syyt'''|the '''causes''' of the accident}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''Syy''' tähän on...|The '''reason''' for this is...}}
# [[reason]], [[cause]] {{gloss|motive for an action or determination}} {{+obj|fi|ill<for>|inf3 ill<to do>}}
#: {{uxi|fi|'''syy''' on pahaa pelätä|there is '''reason''' to be afraid of evil}}
#: {{uxi|fi|On '''syytä''' tietää, että...|It is '''worth''' knowing that...|lit=There is a '''reason''' to know that...}}
#: {{ux|fi|Ei ole '''syytä''' huoleen.|There is no '''cause''' for worry.}}
# [[fault]] {{gloss|blame; responsibility for a mistake}}
#: {{syn|fi|vika}}
#: {{ux|fi|Se on sinun '''syytäsi'''.|It is your '''fault'''.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|reason}} With a nominal ("reason for X"), the nominal is in the illative case (in which case it usually comes after {{m|fi||syy}}) or in the genitive case (in which case it usually comes before {{m|fi||syy}}). With a verb ("reason to X"), the verb is in the first infinitive form.

